# Nothing taken or rendered from the retail game is ever committed: no dats, installers, screenshots, recordings or
# dumps. Players supply their own retail files; a checkout may hold them next to the source, plus a local server with
# secrets. Patterns starting with '/' match at the repository root only; the others match in any folder.
# Check a path with: git check-ignore -v --no-index <path>

# --- The retail game and local setup kept in a checkout (repository root) ---
# The rules for any folder below also catch some of these; they stay listed so narrowing those cannot expose them.
/client/
/install/
/ac1install.exe
/ac-updates.zip
/D3D9.dll
/dgVoodoo.conf

# --- Passwords, in any folder ---
# Not anchored on purpose, so a copy in any folder stays ignored too: the local server's passwords
# (server/setup-server.ps1 writes these to server/runtime/). Keep personal files out of the
# repository by listing them in .git/info/exclude, which is never shared.
secrets.json
mariadb-root.cnf
mariadb-ace.cnf

# --- Local runtime, caches and renders (repository root) ---
# server/runtime/: downloaded ACE and MariaDB, the databases, logs and secrets.json (server/setup-server.ps1)
# cache/: Godot user data (tools/godot.ps1 -IsolateUserData), smoke and hero-video work folders, DAT-derived caches
# docs/screenshots/: renders of the retail data (terrain goldens, interior tour, golden viewpoints, cinematic stills,
#   hero video)
# tools/installer/out/: scratch dumps from the dat readers (acdat.scratch_out_dir)
# vendor-eval/: third-party clones kept for reading
/server/runtime/
/cache/
/docs/screenshots/
/tools/installer/out/
/vendor-eval/

# --- Retail data, binaries, archives and logs, in any folder ---
# Archives are opaque to review, which is how retail data would slip in (the retail updates and ACE's world database
# both arrive as archives), so none are committed. Logs can hold account names and passwords (ACE's packet log dumps
# the login request).
*.dat
*.exe
*.dll
*.pdb
*.zip
*.cab
*.log

# --- Safety net: images and video in any folder ---
# Every Lifestone render shows retail data, so a stray screenshot, texture dump, GIF, Godot Movie Maker frame or
# cinematic capture (.rgba, .mkv) is ignored wherever it lands. Original artwork made for the project is the
# exception: .png, .jpg, .jpeg and .webp still images under docs/assets/ (documentation) and src/Lifestone.Game/assets/
# (the game). Never put a render there. Video and the other formats here (.gif included) are not allow-listed, and the
# rules above (dats, archives, ...) still apply inside both folders.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.gif
*.bmp
*.tga
*.dds
*.exr
*.avi
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.mov
*.webm
*.ogv
*.rgba
!/docs/assets/**/*.png
!/docs/assets/**/*.jpg
!/docs/assets/**/*.jpeg
!/docs/assets/**/*.webp
!/src/Lifestone.Game/assets/**/*.png
!/src/Lifestone.Game/assets/**/*.jpg
!/src/Lifestone.Game/assets/**/*.jpeg
!/src/Lifestone.Game/assets/**/*.webp

# --- Safety net: audio and session recordings, in any folder ---
# Retail sounds decode to .wav (and the dats hold one MP3), so a stray sound dump is ignored wherever it lands, as is a
# session recording (.lsrec), which holds the server's traffic. Golden fixtures and recordings are regenerated under
# cache/ (ignored above) and never committed. No audio format is allow-listed.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.ogg
*.flac
*.lsrec

# --- .NET ---
# MSBuild binary logs (dotnet build -bl) embed every project file and the environment the build read.
bin/
obj/
.vs/
*.user
TestResults/
*.trx
*.binlog

# --- Godot 4 ---
# .godot/ is local only: the import cache and C# build output (.godot/mono/) are regenerated; export_credentials.cfg
# holds per-user export secrets. *.import and *.uid files are source and stay tracked.
.godot/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# --- Editors and OS ---
# Editor folders are per-user (they hold machine paths such as the Godot binary), so none is shared.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- Claude Code: agent worktrees, per-user settings and memory (a shared .claude/settings.json may be committed) ---
/.claude/worktrees/
**/.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
